# scripts/check-i18n-literals.sh's allow-list (T028). One line per allowed
# hit: `path:line:pattern # reason`. path is relative to the repository root
# and line is the line the grep hit reported at the time it was allow-listed
# — a line that moves needs its entry moved with it, which is deliberate: a
# stale entry silently covering for a different, later literal is worse than
# a gate that needs a one-line update alongside the edit that provoked it.
#
# Nothing is allow-listed today: both literals the gate found (nav.templ's
# aria-label="Primary" and controls.templ's <option>Not recorded</option>)
# turned out to be genuine application text and were extracted through
# i18n.T rather than excused here.
